WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:20.764
I am called Theodoros, and I was born 52 years ago here on Chios, the fifth-largest Greek island in a large sea.

2
00:00:20.765 --> 00:00:25.203
Chios has been home to illustrious people such as the poet Homer,

3
00:00:25.204 --> 00:00:31.372
and the island is the only place on earth that grows mastic trees, which produce gum.

4
00:00:31.373 --> 00:00:38.839
But perhaps the island's greatest achievement is that it is the home of Greece's finest red wine.

5
00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:43.584
I am a winemaker, as my grandfather and father were before me.

6
00:00:43.585 --> 00:00:50.843
For over one hundred years, my family has taken care of this vineyard, and we have produced our own wine.

7
00:00:50.844 --> 00:01:03.026
But this year, 355 BC, I am ready to pass on the family legacy to my son Theodorakis, so he can carry on our winemaking tradition.

8
00:01:03.027 --> 00:01:11.525
Legend says that, long ago, the grandson of King Minos of Crete came to Chios and taught the people how to make wine.

9
00:01:11.526 --> 00:01:18.855
I do not know if that is true, but wine has been an integral part of Greek culture for hundreds of years.

10
00:01:18.856 --> 00:01:29.083
This wonderful drink is associated with Dionysus, the god of wine, who inspires artists, philosophers, and ordinary people like me.

11
00:01:29.084 --> 00:01:36.622
We hold many celebrations in his honor, and naturally wine is a major part of the festivities.

12
00:01:36.623 --> 00:01:43.054
Wine grapes love to grow in Chios, because of the weather and the island's many rolling hills.

13
00:01:43.055 --> 00:01:50.092
We plant the vines in the valleys, where they receive ample sunlight and good natural irrigation when it rains.

14
00:01:50.093 --> 00:01:56.335
Our island has warm days and cool nights, perfect weather for ripening grapes,

15
00:01:56.336 --> 00:02:02.070
and my ancestors developed a growing system long ago that takes advantage of this climate.

16
00:02:02.071 --> 00:02:07.815
Since I was very young, I have always carefully monitored my family's vineyard.

17
00:02:07.816 --> 00:02:14.826
Grapevines have several important parts, and I must pay close attention to each part for a successful crop.

18
00:02:14.827 --> 00:02:21.329
The trunk serves the same purpose as the trunk of a tree, providing firm support for the plant.

19
00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:32.002
In Chios we keep the trunk very short, about 55 centimeters high, because the earth provides warmth for the vine during the cool nights.

20
00:02:32.003 --> 00:02:39.278
The head is the main branch of the grapevine at the top of the trunk, where three or four canes grow each year.

21
00:02:39.279 --> 00:02:45.074
The delicious grapes grow on these canes, which I prune at the end of the growing season.

22
00:02:45.075 --> 00:02:54.275
The spurs are other thinner branches that develop at the top of the trunk, and I prune these back to short stubs at the end of the season too.

23
00:02:54.276 --> 00:03:02.230
Making wine is a long and tedious process, and a winemaker must be patient, hardworking, and diligent.

24
00:03:02.231 --> 00:03:08.232
Before harvesting the grapes, we have to clean large wooden vats with boiled seawater,

25
00:03:08.233 --> 00:03:13.376
as it is important that the grapes are stored in the cleanest containers possible.

26
00:03:13.377 --> 00:03:20.862
It takes many days to clean the vats, and then they must be completely dry before we put the grapes in them.

27
00:03:20.863 --> 00:03:29.125
In my vineyard each cluster of grapes is picked by hand, gathered in big baskets, and then thrown into a large vat.

28
00:03:29.126 --> 00:03:32.687
I have more than twenty workers who harvest the grapes.

29
00:03:32.688 --> 00:03:38.519
When the grapes have been harvested, children arrive and climb into the large vats of grapes.

30
00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:43.021
The fun begins when they start stomping on the grapes with their bare feet.

31
00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:48.249
Of course I remind them to wash their little feet before they jump into the vats!

32
00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:55.508
Many of them play games or sing as they crush the grapes into juice and pulp, a mixture called must.

33
00:03:55.509 --> 00:04:00.193
We put the must into clay jars, where it ferments for a long time.

34
00:04:00.194 --> 00:04:06.764
During fermentation the must foams up as the sugar in the grapes gradually turns to alcohol.

35
00:04:06.765 --> 00:04:17.317
But exposure to the air can make the must turn acidic, so I add honey and salt to keep the taste sweet and full of flavor.

36
00:04:17.318 --> 00:04:24.901
These ingredients make it easier to adjust the taste of the wine as it ferments, a process that takes about six months.

37
00:04:24.902 --> 00:04:31.709
When the wine is ready, I get the containers for the wine, called amphorae, delivered to my vineyard.

38
00:04:31.710 --> 00:04:38.067
An amphora is a tall ceramic vase with a handle on each side that makes it easy to carry.

39
00:04:38.068 --> 00:04:46.047
Amphorae provide excellent storage for the wine, and our amphorae are made in the village by Petros, a good friend.

40
00:04:46.048 --> 00:04:53.659
On one handle of each amphora is our special stamp, which shows the origin of the wine and the winemaker's name.

41
00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:58.478
So whoever drinks the wine will know where it came from and who made it.

42
00:04:58.479 --> 00:05:04.580
Ah! Here is Petros, just in time with the amphorae! But wait a moment.

43
00:05:04.581 --> 00:05:09.850
Before I pour the wine into the vases, I must make sure it is ready.

44
00:05:09.851 --> 00:05:15.954
I scoop some wine into a silver cup, dilute it with seawater, and swirl it around.

45
00:05:15.955 --> 00:05:27.448
Here in Chios wine tastes best when diluted, and the sea provides us with exactly what we need to make the wine even more delicious.

46
00:05:27.449 --> 00:05:35.344
Some barbarians drink the wine straight from the amphora, but this practice is frowned upon by polite society.

47
00:05:35.345 --> 00:05:39.276
Drinking pure wine marks one as an uncultured brute.

48
00:05:39.277 --> 00:05:42.508
But let us not dwell on anything unpleasant!

49
00:05:42.509 --> 00:05:48.706
This is my favorite part of making wine—tasting it.

50
00:05:48.707 --> 00:05:58.829
The aroma is already enticing. Ah, the first sip. Yes, it is perfect.

51
00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:05.777
I give permission, and my workers now pour the fermented wine through a cloth into the amphorae,

52
00:06:05.778 --> 00:06:09.462
and the cloth strains any pulp left over from the must.

53
00:06:09.463 --> 00:06:12.869
Theodoros' wine is now ready to be exported.

54
00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:16.714
However, the wine must be drunk within four years.

55
00:06:16.715 --> 00:06:23.948
If not, it will turn into vinegar, which no living creature can stand to swallow.

56
00:06:23.949 --> 00:06:31.443
After the amphorae are filled with wine, they are loaded onto ships and delivered to cities all around the interior sea.

57
00:06:31.444 --> 00:06:40.456
The finest red wines of Chios are truly appreciated by the nobility and elite of Greece, as well as those of Persia and Egypt.

58
00:06:40.457 --> 00:06:49.281
However, as Greek wine is gaining popularity every year, we hope to expand our shipping to lands even farther away.

59
00:06:49.282 --> 00:06:55.554
It is true that many people from other parts of the world are now cultivating their own grapes to make wine.

60
00:06:55.555 --> 00:07:05.384
But no other country will be able to grow grapes that surpass those from the vineyards of Chios!
